# Supply-chain wait: npm will not resolve a version published less than 7 days
# ago (most malicious releases are caught and pulled within days). Matches the
# 7-day cooldown in .github/dependabot.yml. It gates NEW resolutions only
# (`npm install <pkg>`, `npm update`); what package-lock.json already pins
# installs as locked, so `npm ci` and a lockfile install are unaffected
# (checked on npm 11.21.1, 2026-10-19).
#
# npm 11.10+ honours this key; older npm (10.x, which Vercel's Node 22 image
# ships) accepts it silently and ignores it. That is deliberate: there is no
# npm engines floor and no engine-strict here, because together they failed
# every Vercel build with EBADENGINE (PR #89, 2026-10-10). The lockfile is the
# real pin for deploys; this wait protects the machines that change it.
min-release-age=7
